  "_note": "Abandoned vehicles (DESIGN.md \"Vehicles and batteries\"; M5 part 2, agreed with Aaron: four types, more one-off vehicles may come for later scenes). types: each type's look and loot. size: length (front to back), width and height in metres, used for colliders and the interaction spots. parts: placeholder shapes [w, h, l, x, y, z, colour, shape?] in the vehicle's own frame (x to its right, y up, z forward; (x, y, z) is the centre). shape: none for a box; 'wedgeF' a wedge sloping down toward the front (a windscreen), 'wedgeB' sloping down toward the back (a rear window); 'tyre' coloured parts are drawn as round wheels with a hub. colour: 'body' (the vehicle's paint, picked from paints), 'body2' (a second paint, e.g. a police car's lower half) or a key of colours. lamps: unlit boxes (headlights, tail lights, light bars) drawn bright when an alarm flashes. lids: the hinged parts, closed: box [w, h, l, x, y, z] (the hinge is on one of its edges), extra: more boxes [w, h, l, x, y, z, colour] that swing with it (a door's window: Aaron, door and window are one piece), hollow: a dark box shown once it's open (the inside of the boot or the car: Aaron), hinge: 'back', 'front', 'bottom', 'top' or 'frontSide', and angle (radians) fully open. The bonnet opens wide (you pull the battery through it); the boot and doors only open a crack once searched (Aaron). The driver's door is on the left; the passenger door is the same, mirrored, and either one searches the cab. batteryAt: where the battery sits [x, y, z] (seen once the bonnet is up). spots: the words for each hold-X spot. loot: per spot, a loot table like data/loot.json's (items from loot.json; every entry rolled on its own). battery / alarm on a type: the chance it has one, overriding placement and config (Aaron: every police car has an alarm). placement: which types turn up where (weights), by place: 'path' (pulled onto a pathway's verge), a clearing type id or an encounter id; count: how many in that clearing [min, max]; chance: how likely the clearing has any at all; battery / alarm: override the config chances (the campsite's car always has a battery and no alarm, an easy first source next to home); row: lined up like a roadblock.",
